note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note hw.om: READ-ONLY hardware backend for rtl8127.om (rtlrd, rtlwr, rtldly, rtlbar), for the probe tool.
note
note It reads the chip through a read-only map of PCI BAR 2 (sysfs resource2). Omega's mapget reads aligned 32-bit words only, so a byte
note or 16-bit register is read as its 32-bit word and shifted. rtlwr exits 90: nothing here may write to a real chip. A driver that
note writes needs two things Omega does not have at the pinned compiler yet; see docs/GAPS.md.
note Handle of the BAR mapping: hm[0].
global hm long 2

fn rtlrd off ulong w ulong to ulong
base = and off not ulong 3
v = mapget get hm 0 base 4
sh = mul sub off base 8
if eq w 4
ret v
end
if eq w 2
ret and shr v sh 65535
end
ret and shr v sh 255
end
fn rtlwr off ulong w ulong v ulong to void
exit int 90
end
fn rtldly us ulong to void
d = sleepns long mul us 1000
end
fn rtlbar to void
end
